{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795775374,"nonce":"s+I39EQCQzXYvpsKVVZRnQjLBLQ=","title":"An image's shadow is drawn twice","message":"The paint walk draws the box shadow of an image node, as it does for any node. render_images then drew ImageElement.shadow again before the image. A translucent shadow came out darker: a red shadow at alpha 0.5 over blue read as alpha 0.75, in direct, motion and compositor frames. Frames that draw images through render_images_ref (glass, cached replay) drew it once, so the darkness of a shadow also depended on what else was on the page.\n\nThe second draw was the only reader of ImageElement.shadow apart from the check in node_rows that refused to move an image with a shadow by rows, which the second draw needed.\n\nAn element with an image brush background took the same path.","files":null}]}